1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:05,240
Welcome to the third episode of Earthlings
101, the crash course for alien visitors.

2
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:24,690
Let's talk about sex!

3
00:00:24,690 --> 00:00:44,560
So, what is sex?

4
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:48,559
Most species on earth are divided into male
and female specimen.

5
00:00:48,559 --> 00:00:52,390
Sexual reproduction is a process where a male
and a female individual combine their genetic

6
00:00:52,390 --> 00:00:54,489
code to create a new individual.

7
00:00:54,489 --> 00:00:55,960
How does this work?

8
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:58,280
Consider a couple of typical earth animals.

9
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:02,610
Most of their cells contain a double set of
DNA: one from the male parent, and one from

10
00:01:02,610 --> 00:01:03,940
the female one.

11
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:08,310
To be able to reproduce, both male and female
create cells containing only one randomly

12
00:01:08,310 --> 00:01:14,329
mixed set of DNA: Then the male injects his
cells into the female, a process called copulation.

13
00:01:14,329 --> 00:01:18,429
One male cell fusionates with the female one
and creates a full fledged cell with the usual

14
00:01:18,429 --> 00:01:22,680
double set of DNA: This cell is the base for
the new organism which starts now growing

15
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:29,170
- either in an egg, or inside the body of
the female.

16
00:01:29,170 --> 00:01:33,780
Note that the DNA of the parents isn't mixed
to one set of DNA until the new specimen creates

17
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:35,479
its sex cells.

18
00:01:35,479 --> 00:01:39,110
That's why on earth, different species can
interbreed but the offspring won't be able

19
00:01:39,110 --> 00:01:41,590
to reproduce.

20
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:42,789
Scientific advice.

21
00:01:42,789 --> 00:01:47,619
If you want to use human biology to build
bio-computers, don't limit your research to

22
00:01:47,619 --> 00:01:48,619
the brain.

23
00:01:48,619 --> 00:01:54,279
During copulation, a male human ejaculates
about 300 million sperm cells within 5 seconds.

24
00:01:54,279 --> 00:01:59,810
The DNA in each cell consists of 3 billion
base pairs, each one storing 2 bits of information.

25
00:01:59,810 --> 00:02:04,639
This means that a human ejaculation has a
bandwidth of about 40000 terabytes/sec, which

26
00:02:04,639 --> 00:02:08,929
is twelve times more than the bitrate of Xelarian
neuro-cables.

27
00:02:08,929 --> 00:02:12,650
Female earthlings carry their children inside
their body for nine moon cycles.

28
00:02:12,650 --> 00:02:17,819
During this time, they can't make other children,
while the males can run around, hunt, fight,

29
00:02:17,819 --> 00:02:19,739
and copulate with other women.

30
00:02:19,739 --> 00:02:23,450
So the bottleneck for population growth in
a tribe is the number of females, not the

31
00:02:23,450 --> 00:02:25,060
number of males.

32
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:28,310
That's why men are traditionally the hunters
and fighters and protect women and children

33
00:02:28,310 --> 00:02:30,310
with their life.

34
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:35,630
Males are dispensable - even a single male
can impregnante a whole tribe of females.

35
00:02:35,630 --> 00:02:38,550
The question is: why do earthlings have sex?

36
00:02:38,550 --> 00:02:43,120
The answer lies in the human mind, as I explained
it in the first episode: the beast pushes

37
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:47,189
the ego to have sex with a feeling called
desire, and reward sex with another feeling

38
00:02:47,189 --> 00:02:48,400
called pleasure.

39
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:53,090
The niggler, on the other side; enforces rules
of society through feelings like shame and

40
00:02:53,090 --> 00:02:54,470
guilt.

41
00:02:54,470 --> 00:02:57,819
Most human behaviour comes from this power
game between beast and niggler.

42
00:02:57,819 --> 00:03:02,390
But in case of sexuality, the beast disposes
of a trump card: Love, a strong feeling to

43
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:05,049
emotionally attach the human to another earthling.

44
00:03:05,049 --> 00:03:09,730
Love feels good, and right and noble, and
is immune to both reason and remorse.

45
00:03:09,730 --> 00:03:14,269
So, earthlings think that acting out of love
is an excuse for pretty much anything.

46
00:03:14,269 --> 00:03:19,489
In the last episode, we have seen that life
on earth, from photosynthesis to human civilization,

47
00:03:19,489 --> 00:03:22,659
is all about one thing: Spreading the genetic
code.

48
00:03:22,659 --> 00:03:25,239
We might call this the "genetic imperative".

49
00:03:25,239 --> 00:03:27,719
But why did the genetic imperative favour
sex?

50
00:03:27,719 --> 00:03:31,420
Wouldn’t it be more efficient if all specimen
could bear children on their own, without

51
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:33,969
complicated mating rituals and copulation?

52
00:03:33,969 --> 00:03:38,340
The answer may lie in a somewhat special kind
of creatures: parasites.

53
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:42,989
Actually, parasites exist only on earth, because
it's the only planet where the anti-parasite

54
00:03:42,989 --> 00:03:46,159
regulations of the Central Bureaucracy don't
apply.

55
00:03:46,159 --> 00:03:50,469
Of course, those regulations don't hold for
brain suckers, but that's only because brain

56
00:03:50,469 --> 00:03:52,939
suckers kinda run the bureaucracy.

57
00:03:52,939 --> 00:03:57,750
Therefore they are legally not considered
parasites but "authoritarian symbionts".

58
00:03:57,750 --> 00:04:02,900
Parasites are usually small creatures - like
insects, microbes or worms - which live on,

59
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:06,459
or even inside bigger creatures, draining
their resources.

60
00:04:06,459 --> 00:04:10,689
The problem is that parasites grow and reproduce
faster than their hosts, so they can adapt

61
00:04:10,689 --> 00:04:12,459
to any mutation of the host.

62
00:04:12,459 --> 00:04:18,489
So, fighting parasites by mutating is useless,
because the parasites can mutate much faster.

63
00:04:18,489 --> 00:04:22,680
But sexually reproducing animals show huge
differences with each generation.

64
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:26,300
So it's much harder for parasites to adapt
to the ever-changing characteristics of their

65
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:27,300
hosts.

66
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:32,669
So, in a world with gazillions of parasites,
sexuality is a better strategy.

67
00:04:32,669 --> 00:04:35,610
That's why sexuality is so popular on earth.

68
00:04:35,610 --> 00:04:38,080
Almost all species do it...

69
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:40,319
Except for the microbes.

70
00:04:40,319 --> 00:04:44,419
Tips for tourists.

71
00:04:44,419 --> 00:04:49,870
If you want to observe human sexual behaviour,
look for urban zones called red light districts.

72
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:54,460
You might not be able to observe an actual
copulation, but you may see human mating-dances

73
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:57,450
and watch educational films about sexual reproduction.

74
00:04:57,450 --> 00:05:02,930
Now, the interesting thing about sex is that
it alters completely the rules of evolution.

75
00:05:02,930 --> 00:05:04,169
Why is this so?

76
00:05:04,169 --> 00:05:09,490
Well, in natural selection, the most successful
individuals are those who are able to survive.

77
00:05:09,490 --> 00:05:14,729
So, when a mutation is successful, it's usually
because it serves a certain purpose.

78
00:05:14,729 --> 00:05:18,910
But sexual reproduction involves picking a
mate, and evolution pushes the individuals

79
00:05:18,910 --> 00:05:20,910
to be picky about their mates.

80
00:05:20,910 --> 00:05:25,770
In general, female animals are pickier because
they have a limited reproduction capacity.

81
00:05:25,770 --> 00:05:27,539
This is called sexual selection.

82
00:05:27,539 --> 00:05:33,530
So, sexyness - the ability to attract possible
mates - becomes an important factor for evolutionary

83
00:05:33,530 --> 00:05:34,550
success.

84
00:05:34,550 --> 00:05:39,280
This situation creates some sort of "strange
loop": one of the most important factors in

85
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:42,380
sexyness is actually : sexyness.

86
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:45,430
Consider a group of animals where some males
have a tiny tentacle growing out of their

87
00:05:45,430 --> 00:05:46,430
head.

88
00:05:46,430 --> 00:05:49,160
Let's assume some females find this rather
cute.

89
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:52,610
So, males with tentacles become slightly sexier.

90
00:05:52,610 --> 00:05:57,389
The point is, sexy males are likely to have
sexy offspring, and every female wants sexy

91
00:05:57,389 --> 00:06:01,349
offspring, because the sexier the offspring
is, the more he will spread mummy's genetic

92
00:06:01,349 --> 00:06:02,550
code.

93
00:06:02,550 --> 00:06:06,400
In consequence, even the females who were
not interested in tentacles in the first place

94
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:08,940
want now sexy tentaculous offspring.

95
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:12,319
So, tentacles become even more attractive.

96
00:06:12,319 --> 00:06:16,699
So we have entered a strange loop where tentacles
are sexy simply because tentacles are sexy,

97
00:06:16,699 --> 00:06:20,990
without any practical reason other than the
fact that everybody wants sexy offspring.

98
00:06:20,990 --> 00:06:25,460
From generation to generation, tentacles will
grow bigger and bigger until they are so encumbering

99
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:28,350
that they actually reduce the ability to survive.

100
00:06:28,350 --> 00:06:31,169
This example is less exaggerated than it seems.

101
00:06:31,169 --> 00:06:36,069
Some species develop giant encumbering antlers,
or huge colored tail feathers, or elaborate

102
00:06:36,069 --> 00:06:40,240
mating songs.

103
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:44,580
Some scientists even think that human intelligence
has developed as kind of "mental antlers",

104
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:48,380
pushed forward by sexual selection rather
than by the need for survival.

105
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:51,280
Now let's have a closer look at earthling
sexuality.

106
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:54,090
When are earthlings considered to be attractive?

107
00:06:54,090 --> 00:06:58,060
Males are attractive when they are strong,
healthy, aggressive and intelligent, and have

108
00:06:58,060 --> 00:07:01,650
a high social rank, because all this means
that they will be able to protect and feed

109
00:07:01,650 --> 00:07:03,050
their mate and offspring.

110
00:07:03,050 --> 00:07:08,250
Also, a male who spreads his DNA pretty much
anywhere is sexy, because in this case, chances

111
00:07:08,250 --> 00:07:11,770
are that his sons will spread mummy's DNA
pretty much anywhere.

112
00:07:11,770 --> 00:07:15,780
And finally, males should not be so old that
they are likely to die within some years,

113
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:19,379
because then they won't be able to protect
and feed their offspring - except if they

114
00:07:19,379 --> 00:07:23,370
are old and rich, which means that they will
leave a lot of money behind, and money can

115
00:07:23,370 --> 00:07:25,069
buy protection and food.

116
00:07:25,069 --> 00:07:28,410
So, old men are only sexy if they are rich.

117
00:07:28,410 --> 00:07:32,630
For females, the primary selection criterion
is the ability to bear a lot of children before

118
00:07:32,630 --> 00:07:34,430
she runs out of egg cells.

119
00:07:34,430 --> 00:07:37,229
So, health and youth are crucial.

120
00:07:37,229 --> 00:07:40,819
Large hips are sexy because large hip bones
make childbearing easier.

121
00:07:40,819 --> 00:07:45,199
Also, a slim waist is sexy because it means
that the large hips don't just come from an

122
00:07:45,199 --> 00:07:46,900
excess of body fat.

123
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:51,900
And finally, large breasts are sexy because,
well, nobody really knows why.

124
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:56,200
They may just have evolved by the strange
loop of sexual selection, without any particular

125
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:59,169
reason, like antlers or colored tail feathers.

126
00:07:59,169 --> 00:08:04,870
And finally, intelligence and social rank
also add to the attractivity.

127
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:06,479
Strategic advice.

128
00:08:06,479 --> 00:08:10,300
If you want to infiltrate human society with
shape shifters to gather intelligence for

129
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:14,169
an invasion, you may consider your operatives
taking the shape of attractive females.

130
00:08:14,169 --> 00:08:18,759
If you do so, pay attention to details: Even
minor errors like the wrong number of eyes

131
00:08:18,759 --> 00:08:24,110
or the wrong skin color may freak out humans
and compromize your agents.

132
00:08:24,110 --> 00:08:28,091
Spreading the code and choosing partners with
quality DNA are not the only goals: The humans

133
00:08:28,091 --> 00:08:30,979
must also feed and protect their offspring.

134
00:08:30,979 --> 00:08:34,770
Humans usually unite those goals by choosing
one long-term partner to raise the children

135
00:08:34,770 --> 00:08:37,270
with - and then cheating upon him.

136
00:08:37,270 --> 00:08:41,820
For a male earthling, a proven strategy is
to choose one female as long-term partner,

137
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:46,130
and then copulate with lots of other females
behind her back to spread the code.

138
00:08:46,130 --> 00:08:50,100
Society tolerates this behaviour, more or
less, and a man who does so is considered

139
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:51,180
a winner.

140
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:56,160
Women, on the other hand, usually carry one
child at a time, no matter how many sexual

141
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,690
partners they have.

142
00:08:57,690 --> 00:09:01,300
So they better be picky about the DNA of their
children's fathers.

143
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:04,690
That's why society frowns upon women who have
a lot of sexual partners.

144
00:09:04,690 --> 00:09:09,270
A popular female strategy is to choose the
best possible long-term partner, to feed and

145
00:09:09,270 --> 00:09:13,100
protect her offspring - and then cheat upon
him with another male providing high-quality

146
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:15,180
DNA for said offspring.

147
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:19,650
This is often one of the "winners" we mentioned
before, or at least a younger, richer or otherwise

148
00:09:19,650 --> 00:09:21,320
more attractive male.

149
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:25,560
Of course, no male wants to raise the offspring
of a rival, so the cheating has to be done

150
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:26,600
in secret.

151
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:31,330
Again, this behaviour is often more or less
tolerated by society, or even romantically

152
00:09:31,330 --> 00:09:33,700
idealized in fictional works.

153
00:09:33,700 --> 00:09:38,490
Speaking of fictional works: vampires, the
fictional predators mentioned in episode one,

154
00:09:38,490 --> 00:09:43,300
are considered highly attractive, because
they are real experts in feeding and not dying.

155
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:46,830
There is even a popular fictional work about
an underage girl having a relationship with

156
00:09:46,830 --> 00:09:49,320
a vampire who has more than six times her
age.

157
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:53,730
A relationship between humans having this
age difference would never be tolerated by

158
00:09:53,730 --> 00:09:56,850
society, but apparently it's ok if the male
is a vampire.

159
00:09:56,850 --> 00:10:01,320
It should be mentioned that many animal species
have developed same sex copulation, also known

160
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:03,110
as homosexuality.

161
00:10:03,110 --> 00:10:07,360
This has nothing to do with reproduction,
it serves social purposes, for example to

162
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:09,390
resolve social conflicts.

163
00:10:09,390 --> 00:10:14,410
So it is all natural that some humans also
show homosexual behaviour - except for creationists

164
00:10:14,410 --> 00:10:18,690
who claim not to descend from animals.

165
00:10:18,690 --> 00:10:22,380
When earthlings have raised children, one
of their main concerns is often that the offspring

166
00:10:22,380 --> 00:10:24,160
keeps spreading the code.

167
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:28,060
They push their children to look for partners
with high-quality DNA, they encourage them

168
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:33,390
to reproduce, and even tolerant parents tend
to freak out if ever a child reveals as homosexual,

169
00:10:33,390 --> 00:10:37,900
simply because homosexual offspring is a dead
end for the DNA: By the way, the fear of having

170
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:43,230
homosexual offspring is the main reason why
many earthlings think homosexuality is wrong.

171
00:10:43,230 --> 00:10:47,900
Human sexual behaviour, like human behaviour
in general, is mostly determined by genetic

172
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:53,130
programmation - either directly by human nature,
or indirectly by society, which has evolved

173
00:10:53,130 --> 00:10:56,330
with human nature and is hard-wired into the
human brain.

174
00:10:56,330 --> 00:11:01,600
After all, everything comes down to the single
most important driving force of human civilization,

175
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:04,370
the genetic imperative : Spreading the code.

176
00:11:04,370 --> 00:11:08,940
In the next episode we will talk about ethics:
what is good, what is evil, and what has it

177
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:10,830
all to do with eating fruits.

178
00:11:10,830 --> 00:11:14,820
We will also discuss what happens when you
throw Mighty Cthulhu and Great Xenu together

179
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:16,690
in prison.

180
00:11:16,690 --> 00:11:35,930
Thanks for watching.

181
